{
	title: 'A broken plugin is reported to the session that last edited it',
	spec: 'When the plugin loader disables a failing plugin (task 90v renames it to <name>.ts.broken), it tells the session whose declared file edit most recently changed that plugin (task c4x). The message is model-visible, names the original and disabled paths, preserves the complete error and stack, and explains how to enable the file again. Report activity, not ownership: its last declared edit preceded the failure. Gitignored plugins qualify. If no session can be identified, or delivery is refused, show the failure only in the shared notice area in terminal and web, retaining complete details in notice history. Never append such failures to session transcripts or start unrelated sessions. Never guess a writer from timing. Tests cover identified-editor delivery and unidentified failures reaching notices without changing any open session history.',
	status: 'done',
	notes: [
		"src/host/plugin-reports.ts: plugins.report(text, path) on the host. lastEditor scans every existing session's changes.list (after pages catch-up) for the newest declared step on the plugin's canonical path (directory realpath + name, since the file is already renamed). Found: a model-visible message from 'plugin loader' via prompts.submit, else (or if refused) the old notice to every open session and client. A /changes clear in that session hides its edits from the search.",
		'The fallback previously called slash.output for every open session as well as sending a warning. Unknown-source plugin failures now use a shared failed notice and durable notice history only; editor-directed model messages are unchanged.',
		'Keep pluginReports.deliver compatible with warning events: plugin-sync-client uses that transport for comparison failures. Only unattributed loader reports switch to shared notice events.'
